From 738008dad87e7c62c24898a94a6493df70b009b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BESSER STATEC hackathon team <besser@list.lu>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 20:49:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(nn): single-output recurrent layers, training mode and
 multi-target regression

Three defects met while generating a time-series forecaster from a B-UML
NN model:

- An LSTM/GRU/RNN layer with return_type "last" or "full" returns one
  tensor (the generated code is `x, _ = self.rnn(x)`), but
  `_is_multi_output_module` treated every recurrent layer as multi-output,
  so `validate()` demanded an `input_var` on the next layer. This rejected
  BESSER's own reference model `tests/BUML/metamodel/nn/lstm.py` and the
  editor's `lstm_nn.json` template (marked xfail(strict) in
  test_nn_templates.py, waiting for this fix). Only "hidden" and "both"
  return several tensors now.
- The generated PyTorch `train()` never called `model.train()` and
  `evaluate()` never called `model.eval()`, so dropout stayed active and
  batch normalisation kept updating its statistics during evaluation
  (the TensorFlow template already passes `training=`).
- Regression labels were always unsqueezed to (batch, 1). With several
  targets per row (a network returning k values) MSELoss then broadcast
  (batch, 1, k) against (batch, k) and trained on the wrong loss with a
  warning. Labels are unsqueezed only when they are one-dimensional.

Tests: tests/generators/nn/test_nn_rnn_outputs_and_training_mode.py
(fails on 8.1.0, passes with the fix); the strict xfail in
test_nn_templates.py is removed.
